    escalation: 'Si tras corregir servicios y DNS persisten fallos de MachineAccount o KnowsOfRoleHolders → L3 Identity con el dcdiag /v completo. Si la causa raíz es disco o hardware del DC → Infraestructura/Storage con el fabricante (plan de reemplazo).',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, we reviewed the failing health checks reported for the domain controller {{DOMAIN_CONTROLLER}}. We ran the full directory diagnostics, isolated the failing tests and traced them to degraded directory services and incomplete DNS records. The required services were restarted, the DNS records of the controller were validated and replication was confirmed healthy. A new diagnostic run now passes and authentication and policy processing remain normal for users. The before and after outputs are attached to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and monitoring will alert earlier on this condition.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Diagnostic triage on {{DOMAIN_CONTROLLER}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}: dcdiag /v reported failed tests in connectivity and advertising. The System log showed Netlogon errors and the DC DNS records were partially missing. Remediation: Netlogon, kdc and DNS services restarted on the controller, dcdiag /test:dns revalidated the record set, nltest /dsgetdc confirmed the locator returns the correct site server, and repadmin /replsummary shows zero replication errors. Root cause documented as a stale service condition after a previous maintenance window. Evidence archived with the ticket.',
    keywords: ['dcdiag', 'controlador de dominio', 'domain controller', 'health check', 'connectivity', 'advertising', 'netlogon', 'kdc', 'repadmin', 'nltest', 'pruebas fallidas', 'diagnóstico ad', 'dc'],
