    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, as part of the approved change window for ticket {{TICKET_ID}} we transferred the five Active Directory FSMO roles from the retiring domain controller to a healthy one. The operation completed during the maintenance window with no user impact. We verified that the new role holder is replicating correctly, that time and password operations run normally and that new accounts are created without errors. The old controller is now clear for decommissioning under the change plan. The before and after role ownership evidence is attached to the change record.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'FSMO role transfer executed at {{TIMESTAMP}} under change ticket {{TICKET_ID}}: netdom query fsmo initially listed {{DOMAIN_CONTROLLER}} as holder of all five roles. Destination health was validated with dcdiag and replication checks before the move. Move-ADDirectoryServerOperationMasterRole transferred PDCEmulator, RIDMaster, InfrastructureMaster, DomainNamingMaster and SchemaMaster to the target controller. Post-checks: netdom query fsmo reflects the new holders, repadmin /replsummary is clean, w32tm on the new PDC reports a valid upstream time source, and RID allocation was verified with a test account creation that was removed afterwards. No seize was required, so the source controller remains safe for a clean demotion.',
