    escalation: 'Membresías de cuentas desconocidas o cambios sin registro operativo → SOC de inmediato con los eventos (posible compromiso de privilegio). Rediseño de anidamiento de grupos (modelo AGDLP) → L3 Identity.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, we completed the quarterly review of privileged group membership in Active Directory. We exported the full effective membership including nested groups, compared it against the approved baseline and validated each difference with the group owner. Two accounts that no longer required access were removed with documented approval. The final membership now matches the signed approval list and the evidence package, including the membership export and change history, is attached to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} for the audit trail.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Privileged group audit executed at {{TIMESTAMP}}: Get-ADGroupMember with the Recursive switch enumerated the effective membership of {{GROUP}}, and the export was compared with the previous baseline using Compare-Object. Differences were correlated with security event 4728 records to identify who added each member and when. Two stale service accounts and one former employee account were removed with owner approval using Remove-ADGroupMember, and their removal generated fresh audit events. The new baseline export is stored as the comparison input for the next cycle. Recommendations: quarterly revalidation of nested group design and automated alerting on membership changes in tier zero groups.',
    keywords: ['auditoría', 'audit', 'get-adgroupmember', 'recursive', 'domain admins', 'grupo', 'membresía', 'membership', '4728', 'compare-object', 'privilegiado', 'tier zero', 'ex-empleado', 'remove-adgroupmember'],
