    escalation: 'Si el writer fallido es de SQL o de una aplicación → DBA/dueño de la app con el vssadmin list writers. Fallas persistentes del motor WSB → L3 Backup con el log completo; y si el destino es cinta/appliance del fabricante → caso con el fabricante.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hello, we resolved the backup failure affecting this server. The nightly backup had been failing because the volume snapshot service was left in a failed state by one application writer, so no restore points were being created. We verified the backup destination and capacity, restarted the snapshot service, ran an immediate full backup that completed successfully and confirmed the following nightly run created its restore point. The server has current backups again and we attached the evidence of the recovered backup chain to ticket {{TICKET_ID}}.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Windows Server Backup failure on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}: wbadmin get versions showed no new restore points for several days while the Microsoft-Windows-Backup event log recorded nightly errors in the snapshot phase. vssadmin list writers identified one application writer in a failed state blocking VSS snapshots. Remediation: the writer application service was restarted in coordination with its owner, VSS was restarted, target volume capacity was validated with Get-Volume, and an immediate manual backup with wbadmin start backup including all critical volumes completed successfully. The following scheduled run created a new version, restoring a one day RPO. Monitoring now alerts when no new backup version appears within twenty four hours.',
    keywords: ['windows server backup', 'wbadmin', 'backup failure', 'vss', 'vssadmin list writers', 'restore points', 'get-wbpolicy', 'respaldo', 'snapshot', 'rpo', 'volumen', 'falla', 'copia'],
